# {{ site.name }}

> Practical Design Systems is a consultancy and publication by {{ site.author.name }} about building design systems: design tokens, component libraries, Storybook, Figma, governance, adoption, and collaboration between designers, engineers, and stakeholders at organizations with many teams and products.

{{ site.author.name }} has worked in the industry for more than 20 years, both as a solo entrepreneur and in leadership at large organizations. Jesse started in design and moved into engineering, so the writing here covers both high-level strategy for leaders and hands-on guidance for practitioners. Articles started as the Design Systems Daily email newsletter.

## Start here

- [30 Days of Design Systems]({{ site.url }}/30-days/): A free email course covering design system fundamentals, from what a design system is to tokens, components, documentation, governance, and measuring success.
- [Design Systems Daily archive]({{ site.url }}/daily/): Every article, newest first.
- [Services]({{ site.url }}/services/): Design system consulting, workshops, and advisory work from Practical Design Systems.
